entries.what_remains_new:
Content-adaptive playback speed is old: SmartPlayer 2009, US6760536, DIDA. A closed-loop servo on a third-party web player's playbackRate is shipped OSS (Jump Cutter, Silence Cut, Skip Silence; Jump Cutter even has a clone-lookahead and seek mode). An ASR-intelligibility cap on speed is AIx Speed. What remains is a specific combination aimed at a machine perceiver rather than a human:
(1) the controlled variable is surprises per wall second, taken from a visual luma prediction residual, instead of audio silence or offline density scores;
(2) r_max is bounded so the media-time sample density stays at or above opts.fps, using presentedFrames per wall second measured through rVFC;
(3) r_max is backed off when getVideoPlaybackQuality().droppedVideoFrames rises;
(4) a 'regressive saccade' rewinds and replays the window at 1x after a cut detected at high r, so dense keyframes can be taken;
(5) the bored stop is evaluated in media time.
None of these is individually inventive. Their composition into a retina sensor-rate controller for an LLM browsing agent was not found in any paper, patent or repo searched. This is an engineering contribution with a falsifiable benchmark, not a new principle.
